The knowledge packs in this repository's releases are not covered by Dravix's MIT license.

They are derived from the MapleClassic Wiki (https://mapleclassic.wiki/), whose content is
published under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
license (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). They are shared under the same license:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

Attribution: game data from the MapleClassic Wiki contributors, https://mapleclassic.wiki/
Changes: tables were selected, joined and cleaned; training spots were derived from monster
levels and spawns; each monster keeps its five likeliest drops and, from format 3.1, its whole
list; quest texts were shortened.

The rows of a monster's drop list marked "source": "v83" in a pack of format 3.2 or later, and
the mapping they are built from, gms-v83-drops.json in this repository, are a separate work
derived from the GMS v83 drop table of HeavenMS (https://github.com/ronancpl/HeavenMS,
sql/db_drops.sql), which is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
(AGPL-3.0). That work is shared under the same license, whose text is in AGPL-3.0.txt here; the
mapping is its source form. Changes: the table's rows were matched by name to the wiki's monsters
and items, rows bound to a quest, at zero chance, of cards or of items the wiki does not list were
left out, and the rates were not kept. A pack is an aggregate of that work and the wiki's data;
Dravix itself only reads the pack.

The pictures of monsters, items, NPCs and skills in a pack of format 3 or later are NEXON's game
art, as the MapleClassic Wiki shows them, included for identification only. They are covered
neither by the wiki's license, nor by the AGPL, nor by Dravix's; NEXON holds their copyright.

The packs hold no code. MapleStory is a trademark of NEXON Korea Corporation. Dravix is not
affiliated with NEXON, with the MapleClassic Wiki or with HeavenMS.
